  url: {{baseUrl}}/parlance.v1.LocalizationService/BatchTranslate
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "entryIds": [
      "{{entryId1}}",
      "{{entryId2}}",
      "{{entryId3}}"
    ],
    "sourceLocaleId": "en",
    "targetLocaleId": "de"
  }
}

docs {
  # BatchTranslate

  Translates multiple entries at once using AI (DeepL) from source to target locale.

  ## Request
  - `entry_ids` (required): Array of entry IDs to translate
  - `source_locale_id` (required): Locale to translate from (e.g., "en")
  - `target_locale_id` (required): Locale to translate to (e.g., "de")

  ## Response
  - `localizations`: Array of successfully translated localizations
  - `success_count`: Number of successful translations
  - `failure_count`: Number of failed translations

  ## Behavior
  - Processes each entry independently
  - Continues on failure (doesn't stop the batch)
  - For each entry:
    - Creates new localization if it doesn't exist
    - Updates existing localization if it exists
  - Skips entries where source localization is missing

  ## User Tracking
  The authenticated user is recorded as creator/updater for all translations.

  ## Error Codes
  - `INVALID_ARGUMENT`: Missing required fields or empty entry IDs array

  ## Example Use Case
  When adding a new locale to the project, translate all existing entries at once.
  Useful for initial population of a new language.

  ## Performance
  Best for batches of 10-100 entries. For larger datasets, consider chunking.

  ## Note
  Currently returns placeholder "[AI-Translated from source]" prefix.
  TODO: Integrate DeepL API for real batch translations.
}
